<body>

<h1>Manage PIPO</h1>

<div id="overDiv" style="position:absolute; visibility:hidden; z-index:1000;"></div>

<script language="JavaScript" src="overlib.js"></script>

<a name="top">

<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">

<tr><td class="largeheadline"><script language="JavaScript" src="titleline.js"></script></td>

</tr>

</table>

<hr>

<!-- Begin Page Layout -->

<p>The phase in/phase out (PIPO) is the overall process of substituting the
existing stock keeping units (SKU’s) with the new SKU’s. There are two
indicators that assist in the phase-in/phase-out process. The first indicator is
the New Product indicator (NPI) and the second is the End of Life indicator (EOL).</p>

<p>The planners identify from which date they want to start forecasting the new
SKU (phase-in date) and from which date they want to discontinue forecasting for
the old SKU (phase-out date). These dates are captured in the form of the NPI
and EOL indicators.
<br><br></p>

<table class="shadow" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"width="100%" border="0">

<tr>

<td class="tableHeader">&nbsp;What you can do



</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>

            <table class="tableBorder" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="0" width="100%" border="0">

            <tr class="tableRow0">

            <td>

                        <p class="Header2">Search for a PIPO Setup</p>

                        <ol>
                        <li>In the Navigation Pad, you must have clicked on the <b>Manage
                          PIPO</b> &gt; <b>PIPO Setup</b> link to view the current screen.
                        <li>The PIPO Setup screen is displayed.&nbsp;
                        <li>You can perform a search based on the
                          Name, Description, Level Name, EOL Measure Id, NPI
                          Measure Id. Search is case sensitive. Currently only
                          sub-string search is supported.
                        <li>Enter appropriate values in the required search fields and click on&nbsp;
                          <b>Search </b> button.</a>














                        </ol>

                        <blockquote>
                          <blockquote>

                        <b>Note: </b>The value of search string should be
                            name/description of the member. Wildcard search is
                            not supported. To narrow your search
                            list,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can also specify an
                            appropriate status and/or state.
                          </blockquote>
                        </blockquote>
                        <ol start="5">
                          <li>All the records that match the search parameters that you specified will be displayed.<a name="top">














                            </li>
                          </ol>

                        <p class="Header2">Adding a PIPO Setup</p>
                        <ol>
                          <li>To add a PIPO Setup, click the <b>Add</b> button.</li>
                          <li>The Select EOL and EOLLevelID page is displayed.</li>
                          <li>Select an EOL from the list that is displayed.
                            Click Next. If you choose not to mention EOL, then
                            click <b>Skip</b> button. You can skip the
                            selection, in case this setup will be used only to
                            define phase-in (PI). This is provided in order to
                            allow you define phase-ins and copy history from
                            similar SKU's to initiate the forecasting process.</li>
                          <li>The Select NPI and NPILevelID page is displayed.
                            The value that you selected in the previous step is
                            not displayed now.</li>
                          <li>Select a NPI from the list and click <b>Next</b>.</li>
                          <li>Select a dimension from the Select Dimension and
                            Level ID page that is displayed.</li>
                          <li>Enter a meaningful Name and Description and click <b>Save
                            and Return</b> to save the PIPO Setup and return to
                            the main page. A new PIPO Setup ID is created for
                            the parameters you have specified.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p class="Header2">Adding Measure Details</p>
                        <ol>
                          <li>
                            <p class="bodyText">From the PIPO Setup page, click
                            the <b>Add Measure Details</b> button</a>.</li>
                        <li>
                          <p class="bodyText">The Select SourceMeasure ID page
                          is displayed.</li>
                        <li>
                          <p class="bodyText">Select a SourceMeasure ID from the
                          list or search for a SourceMeasure ID by entering one
                          of the search criteria and click <b>Next</b>.</li>
                        <li>
                          <p class="bodyText">Select a TargetMeasure ID from the
                          list or search for a TargetMeasure ID by entering one
                          of the search criteria and click <b>Next</b>.</li>
                        <li>
                          <p class="bodyText">Select a Source Measure Start Date
                          and End Date and Target Measure Start Date (optional)
                          using the Date picker.</li>
                        <li>
                          <p class="bodyText">Click <b>Save And Return</b>. The
                          measure details are saved. You can view the measure
                          details of a PIPO Setup by clicking the <b>Show
                          Measure Details</b> button in the PIPO Setup page.</li>
            </ol>
                            <p class="bodyText">&nbsp;
                            <p class="bodyText">&nbsp;
                        <p>&nbsp;</p>
                        <p>&nbsp;

            </td>

            </tr>

